    "body": "## What breaks\n\n`expand2square` is used by LLaVA, Janus Pro and `process_images`. It only converted `L` images to RGB, and that conversion sat **after** the square-input early return, so:\n\n| input | before |\n|---|---|\n| `L`, square | returned mode `L` (conversion skipped) |\n| `LA`, `I;16`, `1`, non-square | `TypeError: color must be int or tuple` from `Image.new` |\n| `P` | returned the palette image; the three-channel normalize fails later |\n| `RGBA`, `CMYK` | returned a 4-channel image; same downstream failure |\n\nMeasured over 8 PIL modes x {square, non-square}: only non-square `L` worked.\n\nImpact per caller:\n\n- `processors/llava.py` feeds the result straight to `image_processor(image.convert(\"RGB\"))`, so it only suffers the `TypeError` paths;\n- `configs/janus_pro.py` does `np.transpose(x, (2, 0, 1))` assuming `[H, W, 3]`, so L/P/I;16 produce a wrong-shaped array;\n- `mm_utils.process_images` passes the result to `image_processor.preprocess` with no conversion, so the non-RGB modes fail at normalize.\n\n## Fix\n\n```python\n-    if width == height:\n-        return pil_img\n-    if pil_img.mode == \"L\":\n-        pil_img = pil_img.convert(\"RGB\")\n+    if pil_img.mode != \"RGB\":\n+        pil_img = pil_img.convert(\"RGB\")\n+    if width == height:\n+        return pil_img\n```\n\nAny non-RGB mode is converted before the early return. `convert(\"RGB\")` matches what `llava.py` already did explicitly; for `LA`/`RGBA` the alpha channel is dropped, which is the pre-existing behaviour of that call site. `smart_to_rgb` would composite against a sampled background instead — happy to switch if you prefer that.\n\n## Tests\n\n`test/registered/unit/multimodal/test_expand2square_modes.py`: 8 modes x 2 sizes plus a padding/content assertion.\n\n- unpatched: **13 failed, 4 passed**\n- patched: **17 passed**\n\n`ruff check` and `ruff format --check` clean on both files.\r\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39276138243](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39276138243)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39276138062](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39276138062)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39276138162](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39276138162)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
